# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Control an opponent's library search, exile its chosen card, and cast it.
# Forcing: The required creature begins only in the opponent's library.
# AI behavior: Empty hand and battlefield leave no competing choices.
# Failure modes: A missing search blocks resolution; a library card disproves replacement;
#   a missing cast action disproves permission to use the exiled card.
# Card roles: Agent controls the search; Symmetry searches both libraries; Bears is the chosen spell.
# Protocol path: Target selection, two searches, exile replacement, and casting.
[metadata]
Name:Opposition Agent Search
Goal:Play the Specified Permanent
Targets:Card.namedGrizzly Bears
Turns:4
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Search both libraries with Scheming Symmetry and cast the opponent's exiled Bears.
